<DocsLayout title="Quick start: reachability" kicker="08 / tutorial" description="Build a deterministic shortcut set and verify that it preserves exact reachability.">
  <h2>One invariant, two traversals</h2>
  <p>Run a direct BFS and a traversal over the original graph plus shortcuts. The result should be identical for the same source.</p>
  <pre><code>from reachq.generators import random_dag
from reachq.invariants import assert_reachability_preserved
from reachq.reachability import bfs_reachability, parallel_bfs
from reachq.shortcut import build_shortcut_set_for_reachability

graph = random_dag(100, edge_probability=0.1, random_seed=42)
shortcuts, beta, bound = build_shortcut_set_for_reachability(
    graph, omega=3.0, random_seed=42,
)
assert_reachability_preserved(graph, shortcuts)
source = graph.vertices()[0]
assert parallel_bfs(graph, source, shortcuts) == bfs_reachability(graph, source)</code></pre>
  <p>See the <a href="/reachq/limitations.html">adoption boundary</a> before interpreting the construction as a practical speedup.</p>
</DocsLayout>
